      "explanation": "Role 2: accessibility worker. It first delegates to IsAnySymbolAccessible (line 845), which performs accessible-chain discovery via getAccessibleSymbolChain and getContainersOfSymbol and asks the emit resolver's hasVisibleDeclarations for visible declarations and AliasesToMakeVisible (symbolaccessibility.go:26-103). If that yields a non-nil result it returns it. Only when the chain search is exhausted does it classify the failure: it finds the symbol's external-module container (core.FirstNonNil + getExternalModuleContainer, line 852) and, if that differs from the enclosing declaration's external module, reports SymbolAccessibilityCannotBeNamed (an unexported name from a different external module, lines 855-863); otherwise it reports SymbolAccessibilityNotAccessible for an inaccessible local name (867-870). It is reached from the tracker through the EmitResolver.IsSymbolAccessible adapter (emitresolver.go:685, lock + checker call) and from the isEntityNameVisible/hasVisibleDeclarations path (emitresolver.go:334-465)."
