      "explanation": "Role 4: accessibility-result consumer. When the result is Accessible it appends every AliasesToMakeVisible entry onto state.lateMarkedStatements via core.AppendIfUnique (lines 205-211) — this is what enqueues newly visible internal import aliases. When the result is SymbolAccessibilityNotResolved it does nothing (no diagnostic), because the checker already reports unresolvable names (215 comment). For any other status (NotAccessible or CannotBeNamed) it consults the context-dependent provider state.getSymbolAccessibilityDiagnostic and, if present, emits either the typed or untyped diagnostic and returns true (215-231). getSymbolAccessibilityDiagnostic and errorNameNode are installed per enclosing node by setupDiagnosticContext (transform.go:551-571), which is the 'context-dependent diagnostic' mechanism; throwDiagnostic (transform.go:276) is the sentinel used outside a valid diagnostic context."
